2015-05-18 16:04  reyk

	* libexec/spamd/: grey.c, sdl.c, spamd.8, spamd.c: Change spamd to
	  use divert-to instead of rdr-to.

	  divert-to has many advantages over rdr-to for proxies.  For
	  example, it is much easier to use, requires less code, does not
	  depend on /dev/pf, works in-band without the asynchronous lookup
	  (DIOCNATLOOK ioctl), saves us from additional port allocations by
	  the rdr/NAT code, and even avoids potential collisions and race
	  conditions that could theoretically happen with the lookup.

	  Heads up: users will have to update their spamd PF rules from
	  rdr-to to divert-to.	spamd now also listens to 127.0.0.1 instead
	  of "any" (0.0.0.0) by default which should be fine with most
	  setups but has to be considered for some special configurations.

	  Based on a diff is almost two years old but got delayed several
	  times ... beck@: "now is the time to get it in" :)

	  Tested by many With help from okan@ OK okan@ beck@ millert@

