	  usr.sbin/spamdb/spamdb.8, usr.sbin/spamdb/spamdb.c: Add -g option
	  for greylisting support for spamd. The greylisting techinque
	  originates from a paper by Evan Harris which can be found at
	  http://projects.puremagic.com/greylisting/. This implementation
	  makes spamd allow for non-blacklisted addresses to be treated as
	  "greylisted".  where they are tracked in a db file, and
	  whitelisted by addition to a pf table when the same envelope from
	  and to are retried from the same source IP address. Testing by
	  many, ok deraadt@

